constant factor rule,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int -\\frac{5}{2}\\sec^2 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n&=-\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\sec^2 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\\n&=-\\frac{5}{2}\\tan t+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe negative factor remains negative. Differentiating the answer gives $-\\frac{5}{2}\\sec^2 t$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1187f774-e426-56b3-8d7d-aa6c9aaccc20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan x-\\sec x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720990} {:answer/id #uuid "33bdd6af-bedd-5fe0-b589-8dd07a92ff39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan x-\\sec x+\\cos x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720994} {:answer/id #uuid "6050958b-fef0-5c2d-8b5e-2f2137dc84ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan x+\\sec x+\\cos x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720997} {:answer/id #uuid "7eee5d70-459d-58b9-b999-23261a0f0aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan x-\\sec x-\\cos x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721000} {:answer/id #uuid "df636355-97d0-5e2b-8a8c-d4cde6f72fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec x-\\tan x+\\cos x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33bdd6af-bedd-5fe0-b589-8dd07a92ff39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan x-\\sec x+\\cos x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720994} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdcc20f5-55d2-5830-b0ef-f70068aab3ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4df90c70-1e0a-5e66-9228-79b189cee5c8" :question/problem "Calculate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left[\\sec x(2\\sec x-\\tan x)-\\sin x\\right]\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First distribute the secant factor to expose the familiar integrands:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\sec x(2\\sec x-\\tan x)-\\sin x \\\\\n&=2\\sec^2 x-\\sec x\\tan x-\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nRecall that\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\sec^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\tan x+C, \\\\\n\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\sec x+C, \\\\\n\\int \\sin x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=-\\cos x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nApply the sum and constant factor rules, keeping the subtraction signs:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int [\\sec x(2\\sec x-\\tan x)-\\sin x]\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=2\\int \\sec^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&\\quad-\\int \\sin x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=2\\tan x-\\sec x-(-\\cos x)+C \\\\\n&=2\\tan x-\\sec x+\\cos x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe final cosine term is positive because the integral of sine is negative cosine. Differentiating the result gives $2\\sec^2 x-\\sec x\\tan x-\\sin x$, which is the expanded integrand."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ddb7d13-a3a9-5de0-887f-e45a3dcbf136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan x-2\\sec x\\tan x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720996} {:answer/id #uuid "72f8516c-d775-560c-a57e-dc19f3549438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sec x-2\\tan x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720998} {:answer/id #uuid "96fb1412-f242-5d7b-898d-9254996a9e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan x+2\\sec x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721004} {:answer/id #uuid "a011437c-93b0-581c-9b3d-62a34a0f7827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan x-2\\sec x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721005} {:answer/id #uuid "bda35b54-53be-5f28-bb8e-5f212087dd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\tan x-2\\sec x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a011437c-93b0-581c-9b3d-62a34a0f7827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\tan x-2\\sec x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721005} :answer-field/id #uuid "93a82561-e174-5b2d-96d7-32caf55625b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fb81b535-f2ab-596e-bd66-83728ec1ed7c" :question/problem "Calculate\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left(3\\sec^2 x-2\\sec x\\tan x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\sec^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\tan x+C, \\\\\n\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\sec x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int (3\\sec^2 x-2\\sec x\\tan x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3\\int \\sec^2 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x-2\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3\\tan x-2\\sec x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nDifferentiating gives $3\\sec^2 x-2\\sec x\\tan x$. Only one arbitrary constant is needed for the combined antiderivative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09efafa3-9ce3-56d0-857a-5b0708b67530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cot x-3\\csc x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721019} {:answer/id #uuid "15c84a60-6f0c-5d24-bdce-074d2478396c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cot x+3\\csc x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721020} {:answer/id #uuid "5d60cd8a-e3db-53f4-8e63-9965af89154b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\tan x+3\\csc x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721024} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cbdd0e-4587-59c9-8372-1a26d2ab45ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cot x+3\\sec x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721033} {:answer/id #uuid "cb88e3a4-fc71-5819-af7c-854ff84c9df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cot x+3\\csc x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb88e3a4-fc71-5819-af7c-854ff84c9df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cot x+3\\csc x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721035} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3c57676-89f6-5e1c-a8af-592af0b6b8b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3ba10523-e25e-5f96-ae5f-1ac04720ce5d" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\csc x(2\\csc x-3\\cot x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\csc^2x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=-\\cot x+C, \\\\ \\int\\csc x\\cot x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=-\\csc x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $I$ be the requested integral. Expand the product to expose the two familiar forms:\n\n$$\nI=\\int(2\\csc^2x-3\\csc x\\cot x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIntegrate each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=2\\int\\csc^2x\\,\\mathrm{d}x-3\\int\\csc x\\cot x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2(-\\cot x)-3(-\\csc x)+C \\\\ &=-2\\cot x+3\\csc x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186721026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2884b5d0-39d2-5426-b303-09e15a551762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\cot\\theta+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186721021} {:answer/id #uuid "349476f9-23e7-52b0-a582-2cd7591742d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186